   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "$|x||x - 2| - |x - 1| - 6 = 0$ and sum of real solution of $x$.",
   "correct_key": null,
   "correct_value": 2,
   "correct_keys": null,
   "solution": "$x \\ge 2$;\n$x(x - 2) - x + 1 - 6 = 0$\n$x^{2} - 3x - 5 = 0$\n$x = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{29}}{2}$\n$x_{1} = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{29}}{2}$\nII. $1 < x < 2$\n$x(2 - x) - x + 1 - 6 = 0$\n$-x^{2} + x - 5 = 0$\n$x^{2} - x + 5 = 0$\n$D < 0$ (No Solution).\nIII. $0 < x < 1$\n$x(2 - x) + x - 1 - 6 = 0$\n$2x - x^{2} + x - 7 = 0$\n$-x^{2} + 3x - 7 = 0$\n$x^{2} - 3x + 7 = 0$\n$D > 0$ (No Solution)\nIV. $x < 0$\n$x^{2} - x - 1 - 6 = 0$\n$x^{2} - x - 7 = 0$\n$x = \\frac{+1 \\pm \\sqrt{29}}{2}\\ \\therefore x_{2} = \\frac{+1 - \\sqrt{29}}{2}$,\nHence sum of solution\n$= x_{1} + x_{2}$\n$= \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{29} + 1 - \\sqrt{29}}{2}$\n$= 2$",
