  {
   "q_no": 12,
   "topic": "Differential Equations",
   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "$f(x) = \\lim_{t \\to x} \\frac{t^{2}f(x) - x^{2}f(t)}{t - x}$, $f(1) = 1$, find the value of $2f(2) + 3f(3)$",
   "correct_key": null,
   "correct_value": 20,
   "correct_keys": null,
   "solution": "$f'(x) = \\lim_{t \\to x} \\frac{2tf(x) - x^{2}f'(t)}{1}$\n$f'(x) = 2xf(x) - x^{2}f'(x)$\n$\\Rightarrow f'(x) = \\frac{2xf(x)}{1 + x^{2}}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\int \\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)}dx = \\int \\frac{2x}{1 + x^{2}}dx$\n$\\Rightarrow \\ln(f(x)) = \\ln\\left|1 + x^{2}\\right| + c$\n$c = -\\ln 2$\n$\\Rightarrow \\ln(f(x)) = \\ln\\left(\\frac{1 + x^{2}}{2}\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\left\\{f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(1 + x^{2}\\right)\\right\\}$\n$\\Rightarrow f(2) = 5/2, f(3) = \\frac{10}{2}$\n$\\Rightarrow f(2) + 3f(3) = 5 + \\frac{30}{2} = 20$",
